# database backups — these contain LIVE CREDENTIALS, not just user data:
# users.password (bcrypt), users.apple_refresh_token, device_tokens.token,
# sensor_devices.api_key, password_reset_tokens.token. scripts/dump-db.js
# additionally refuses to write anywhere but here. Never commit one.
backend/backups/
*.sql.gz
*.dump

# runtime upload staging. Nothing writes here since the round-12 move to
# in-memory buffering, but if anything ever does, the file must not be
# committed — user photo UGC is not repo content.
backend/uploads/*
!backend/uploads/.gitkeep

# ML training artifacts
backend/scripts/ml/train/*.csv
backend/scripts/ml/train/*.pkl
backend/scripts/ml/train/plots/
backend/scripts/ml/models/incumbent/*.pkl
backend/scripts/ml/models/incumbent/*.json
# The preserved previous model, kept so quick_eval.py can score the incumbent on
# the SAME holdout as a challenger. It is a local artifact of a retrain, not
# source: best_model.pkl is 12MB and features_holdout.pkl is 183MB. RETRAIN.md
# step 0 says how to populate it, and the gate FAILS rather than shrugging when
# it is absent, so an unpopulated directory can never quietly skip the check.

# NOT ignored: backend/scripts/ml/models/crowd_model.onnx is the SHIPPING model.
# It was committed before this rule existed, and git ignores .gitignore for
# already-tracked files, so the rule was inert and the model kept deploying. It
# was also a trap: one `git rm --cached` and the 11MB model silently stops
# shipping, mlPredictor finds no artifact, and production falls back to the rule
# engine forever with no error anyone would notice. The rule is removed rather
# than left sitting there looking authoritative.

# ML collection-run scratch output (local only)
backend/collection_log*.txt
backend/transient_failed_venues.txt
backend/scripts/ml/models/spot_check.py

# local training run logs
backend/scripts/ml/train/train_v*.log
backend/scripts/ml/train/train_v*.err

# Security review working notes (do not commit)
REVIEW-ROUND*-gpt56sol.md
frontend/ios/App/App/GoogleService-Info.plist
frontend/ios/App/App/GoogleService-Info.plist.b64

